WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.242
Hi, I'm Tangerine!

00:00:02.242 --> 00:00:06.367
A swarm of agents can ask a decision model everything in one call.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:09.541
Here's how that works, and where the teamwork really lives.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.505
The expensive half of a decision is the state.

00:00:13.505 --> 00:00:17.763
Ten agents looking at one world send ten questions against one copy of it.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.051
Ten snakes share one arena.

00:00:22.051 --> 00:00:27.654
Before anything is asked, code measures every move: food distance, reachable cells, dead-end risk.

00:00:28.074 --> 00:00:31.851
Each tick sends one request: the state once, plus ten short questions.

00:00:31.851 --> 00:00:34.998
Ten answers come back in roughly the time of one.

00:00:35.418 --> 00:00:37.607
Each snake gets its own probabilities.

00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:40.525
By design, no question can see another's answer.

00:00:40.945 --> 00:00:42.996
So coordination happens in code.

00:00:42.996 --> 00:00:47.918
A resolver enumerates joint moves, drops the illegal ones, and keeps the

00:00:47.918 --> 00:00:50.790
likeliest combination, in about half a millisecond.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.530
How often it overrules the model is the honest diagnostic.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.186
In the published run, two point two percent.

00:00:58.483 --> 00:01:02.937
Grouped against one shared state, the choice readout barely moved: two hundred

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:05.535
sixty-nine of two hundred seventy answers agreed.

00:01:05.955 --> 00:01:09.593
The score readout, a weighted mean over a rubric, shifted about zero

00:01:09.593 --> 00:01:10.806
point two nine levels.

00:01:10.806 --> 00:01:13.838
The winner survives a shift that a mean does not.

00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:18.784
A batch shares the state, not the answers: coordination is code, and

00:01:18.784 --> 00:01:20.982
only the score readout shows the drift.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.659
To recap: share the state, resolve in code, and check the scores.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.982
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:29.982 --> 00:01:30.620
I'm Tangerine.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:30.939
Bye!
